1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,970
Last time, we planted a mango seed, and we observed it like

2
00:00:03,990 --> 00:00:05,130
a scientist.

3
00:00:05,640 --> 00:00:07,220
It grew into a young plant.

4
00:00:07,720 --> 00:00:10,190
But will our young plant ever grow mangoes?

5
00:00:13,148 --> 00:00:15,958
A little weaver ant is hiding in this video.

6
00:00:16,218 --> 00:00:17,448
Can you spot it?

7
00:00:17,569 --> 00:00:20,599
It is very small, and it hides somewhere new each time.

8
00:00:20,699 --> 00:00:22,899
Look along the leaves and the branches!

9
00:00:23,029 --> 00:00:24,869
Lock in first with your fingers.

10
00:00:25,139 --> 00:00:26,969
One finger for every point.

11
00:00:27,556 --> 00:00:28,886
Today you'll learn:

12
00:00:29,083 --> 00:00:30,953
The 3 plant stages.

13
00:00:31,155 --> 00:00:33,105
No first or last stage.

14
00:00:33,306 --> 00:00:34,936
Why seeds are saved.

15
00:00:36,689 --> 00:00:37,569
Round one.

16
00:00:37,879 --> 00:00:41,129
This old mango tree is covered in tiny flowers.

17
00:00:41,399 --> 00:00:42,829
Which stage is it in?

18
00:00:43,129 --> 00:00:44,219
One, the seed.

19
00:00:44,489 --> 00:00:45,839
Two, the young plant.

20
00:00:46,109 --> 00:00:47,719
Three, the adult plant.

21
00:00:47,999 --> 00:00:49,479
Show me with your fingers.

22
00:00:54,949 --> 00:00:55,929
Locked in!

23
00:00:56,057 --> 00:00:56,937
Two.

24
00:00:57,107 --> 00:00:59,647
It still grows new leaves, so I think it is a young

25
00:00:59,667 --> 00:01:00,427
plant.

26
00:01:00,476 --> 00:01:01,216
Three!

27
00:01:01,316 --> 00:01:04,146
Our young plant has no flowers, but this tree does.

28
00:01:04,336 --> 00:01:05,886
So it is an adult plant!

29
00:01:05,941 --> 00:01:06,541
Three!

30
00:01:06,901 --> 00:01:09,461
A plant with flowers must be all grown up.

31
00:01:10,414 --> 00:01:11,564
Look closer.

32
00:01:12,164 --> 00:01:14,874
Here is our young plant, beside the old tree.

33
00:01:14,894 --> 00:01:17,754
Our young plant has a thin stem, but the old tree has

34
00:01:17,774 --> 00:01:20,432
a thick trunk and lots of tiny flowers!

35
00:01:20,452 --> 00:01:21,612
But look at the tips.

36
00:01:21,982 --> 00:01:24,782
The old tree has new red leaves too, so it is still

37
00:01:24,802 --> 00:01:25,632
growing.

38
00:01:25,683 --> 00:01:28,623
The young plant grew into an adult plant.

39
00:01:29,213 --> 00:01:32,803
The adult plant started to have flowers and fruits.

40
00:01:33,928 --> 00:01:35,688
Adult plants keep growing too.

41
00:01:35,808 --> 00:01:39,828
But only a grown-up plant, an adult plant, has flowers and fruits!

42
00:01:42,458 --> 00:01:44,888
The answer is three: the adult plant!

43
00:01:45,178 --> 00:01:46,248
Three fingers?

44
00:01:46,518 --> 00:01:47,728
One finger up!

45
00:01:48,004 --> 00:01:50,201
But where do new mango seeds come from?

46
00:01:50,221 --> 00:01:51,141
From the roots!

47
00:01:51,221 --> 00:01:53,401
The tree pushes them out, under the ground.

48
00:01:53,531 --> 00:01:54,731
Let's find out.

49
00:01:54,991 --> 00:01:56,311
Be a mango flower!

50
00:01:56,631 --> 00:01:57,611
Shrink down.

51
00:01:57,891 --> 00:01:58,821
Quietly.

52
00:02:01,110 --> 00:02:04,080
You are a tiny flower on the big mango tree.

53
00:02:04,860 --> 00:02:08,240
Your petals fall, and you start to grow into a tiny green

54
00:02:08,260 --> 00:02:09,060
mango.

55
00:02:09,582 --> 00:02:12,332
Week after week, you grow bigger and heavier.

56
00:02:13,132 --> 00:02:16,222
Inside you, a seed grows, big and flat.

57
00:02:16,739 --> 00:02:18,409
You turn yellow and sweet.

58
00:02:19,179 --> 00:02:22,319
You are a ripe mango, with a new seed inside!

59
00:02:24,428 --> 00:02:25,098
Oops!

60
00:02:25,198 --> 00:02:28,328
The new seeds grow inside the fruits, not in the roots!

61
00:02:28,449 --> 00:02:30,109
Let me put them on our board.

62
00:02:30,299 --> 00:02:33,309
The seed, then the young plant, then the adult plant, and its

63
00:02:33,329 --> 00:02:34,991
fruits bring new seeds.

64
00:02:35,011 --> 00:02:38,511
So a plant's life cycle goes round and round, and it has

65
00:02:38,531 --> 00:02:39,801
three stages.

66
00:02:40,981 --> 00:02:42,131
Say it with me!

67
00:02:42,846 --> 00:02:45,726
There are three stages in the life cycle of a plant.

68
00:02:46,346 --> 00:02:49,846
The stages are the seed, the young plant and the adult plant.

69
00:02:53,470 --> 00:02:54,370
Showdown!

70
00:02:54,680 --> 00:02:55,810
Double points.

71
00:02:56,080 --> 00:02:58,320
Momo's homework has one mistake.

72
00:02:58,600 --> 00:03:00,380
Line one, two, or three?

73
00:03:00,670 --> 00:03:02,140
Show me with your fingers.

74
00:03:02,202 --> 00:03:03,662
Here is my homework!

75
00:03:03,812 --> 00:03:07,592
Three: the adult plant is the last stage, and the cycle ends.

76
00:03:13,205 --> 00:03:14,185
Locked in!

77
00:03:14,313 --> 00:03:15,053
Three!

78
00:03:15,133 --> 00:03:18,253
The adult plant has fruits with new seeds, so round it goes

79
00:03:18,273 --> 00:03:19,053
again!

80
00:03:19,107 --> 00:03:23,247
Three. A life cycle goes round and round, so there is no last

81
00:03:23,267 --> 00:03:24,187
stage.

82
00:03:25,646 --> 00:03:28,376
The stages in a life cycle are repeated.

83
00:03:28,656 --> 00:03:30,656
There is no first or last stage.

84
00:03:31,176 --> 00:03:32,266
Three fingers?

85
00:03:32,506 --> 00:03:34,436
Put up two more on your score hand!

86
00:03:34,786 --> 00:03:36,916
But what if a kind of plant had no more seeds at

87
00:03:36,936 --> 00:03:37,571
all?

88
00:03:37,591 --> 00:03:38,111
Easy!

89
00:03:38,421 --> 00:03:40,641
Then we just buy more seeds at the shop!

90
00:03:40,690 --> 00:03:45,050
Life cycles repeat to ensure that living things continue to live.

91
00:03:45,320 --> 00:03:48,280
With no seeds, that kind of plant could disappear.

92
00:03:49,063 --> 00:03:50,261
Look closer.

93
00:03:50,281 --> 00:03:57,147
In 2019, Singapore opened its first seed bank, at the Botanic Gardens.

94
00:03:57,829 --> 00:04:01,858
Scientists dry the seeds, and they keep them in jars with labels.

95
00:04:01,878 --> 00:04:05,018
Then the jars go into a very cold room, like a giant

96
00:04:05,038 --> 00:04:08,168
freezer, so the seeds can wait for many years!

97
00:04:10,868 --> 00:04:12,168
Say it with me!

98
00:04:12,879 --> 00:04:16,249
A seed bank stores seeds safely until they are needed.

99
00:04:19,006 --> 00:04:20,111
Say it with us!

100
00:04:20,771 --> 00:04:22,041
Seed, young plant!

101
00:04:22,351 --> 00:04:23,495
Adult plant!

102
00:04:27,171 --> 00:04:28,448
Flowers, fruits!

103
00:04:28,751 --> 00:04:30,020
Seeds inside!

104
00:04:33,571 --> 00:04:34,971
No first, no last!

105
00:04:35,151 --> 00:04:36,374
Round and round!

106
00:04:40,726 --> 00:04:42,196
Show me your score hand!

107
00:04:42,476 --> 00:04:43,526
More than one?

108
00:04:43,826 --> 00:04:45,186
You beat the Buddies.

109
00:04:45,486 --> 00:04:46,546
Three fingers?

110
00:04:46,816 --> 00:04:47,826
High five!

111
00:04:48,331 --> 00:04:49,961
Did you spot the weaver ant?

112
00:04:50,231 --> 00:04:52,751
It was on a leaf of the old mango tree!

113
00:04:52,884 --> 00:04:54,184
Here is a fun fact!

114
00:04:54,244 --> 00:04:57,464
Weaver ants sew leaves together to make their nest, and the sticky

115
00:04:57,484 --> 00:04:59,554
thread comes from their own babies!

116
00:04:59,824 --> 00:05:02,984
They live in mango trees, high up in their leaf nests.

117
00:05:03,112 --> 00:05:04,392
Tell someone at home!

118
00:05:05,181 --> 00:05:06,991
Next time: a tadpole!

119
00:05:07,281 --> 00:05:09,601
It lives in water, and it has a tail.

120
00:05:09,881 --> 00:05:11,121
What will it grow into?

121
00:05:11,531 --> 00:05:12,591
One, a fish.

122
00:05:12,881 --> 00:05:13,951
Two, a frog.

123
00:05:14,221 --> 00:05:15,541
Three, a lizard.

124
00:05:15,801 --> 00:05:17,131
Lock in your answer!

125
00:05:17,409 --> 00:05:19,609
Let's read today's key words together!

126
00:05:19,899 --> 00:05:20,659
Ready?

127
00:05:20,946 --> 00:05:22,106
Adult plant.

128
00:05:23,669 --> 00:05:24,889
Three stages.

129
00:05:26,521 --> 00:05:27,541
Seed bank.

130
00:05:28,982 --> 00:05:29,922
Well done!

131
00:05:30,904 --> 00:05:32,005
Say it with us!

132
00:05:32,805 --> 00:05:33,555
Ready?

133
00:05:33,679 --> 00:05:34,339
One!

134
00:05:34,679 --> 00:05:35,379
two!

135
00:05:35,684 --> 00:05:36,859
Now you know!
